This plugin includes material adapted from the On-Call Kit
(https://github.com/anthropics/oncall-kit), Copyright 2026 Anthropic PBC,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Adapted files keep their original copyright and SPDX headers and carry a
note describing what Reactor Studio changed for Kopai ("Modified by
Reactor Studio for Kopai", or for new files written in the kit's
structure, a note naming what they follow). Each on-call skill folder
also carries a copy of the license as LICENSE.txt. The adaptations:

- oncall-skills/kopai-oncall-playbooks
                              from skills/oncall-setup, plus templates/,
                              eval/replay.md and ONBOARD.md
- oncall-skills/kopai-oncall-setup/references/tag-setup.md
                              from TAG-SETUP.md
- oncall-skills/kopai-triage         from skills/triage (failure-class references
                              rewritten for service telemetry in Kopai)
- oncall-skills/kopai-handoff        from skills/handoff
- oncall-skills/kopai-weather        from skills/weather
- oncall-skills/kopai-oncall-playbooks/templates/ONCALL-RULES.md
                              from the standing rules in CLAUDE.md
- oncall-skills/kopai-verify-fix     new; expands step 9 of skills/triage
- oncall-skills/kopai-evidence-page  new; a snapshot page, only on request
- oncall-skills/kopai-oncall-setup   new; connects one alert channel and creates
                              its watch routine
- oncall-skills/kopai-triage/references/
                              new content for Kopai, in the structure of
                              the kit's triage references

Main changes: skills are renamed with a kopai- prefix; telemetry
capabilities (metrics, logs, traces) bind to the Kopai MCP connector;
team-specific playbooks live in the team's own repository instead of the
plugin; and the standing rules ship as ONCALL-RULES.md, which setup copies
into the team's repository. Kopai is also the alerting tool: triage reads
Kopai alerts by event id, and rule proposals use Kopai's rule editor link.

The skills in skills/ and claude-skills/ are Reactor Studio's own, written
for Kopai.
